(Aeration Basin Retrofit at Greenfield Water Reclamation Plant Design Report, Revision C) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Greenfield Water Reclamation Plant treats wastewater for a service area of 48,000) Tj
T*
(residents. Its two aeration basins were commissioned in 1987 and have operated) Tj
T*
(continuously since. Dissolved oxygen in Basin 2 has fallen below the permitted floor of) Tj
T*
(2 milligrams per litre on 31 days in the past year, each time during the summer peak.) Tj
T*
(The plant operator recorded the longest single excursion as 9 hours.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The cause is not the blowers, which were replaced in 2019 and still meet their rated) Tj
T*
(output. It is the diffuser grid on the basin floor. The original coarse-bubble diffusers) Tj
T*
(transfer oxygen at roughly 1.2 kilograms per kilowatt-hour under clean water conditions,) Tj
T*
(and the membranes have fouled unevenly, so a third of the grid now delivers most of the) Tj
T*
(air. Short-circuiting carries that air to the surface before it dissolves.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Left alone, the plant will breach its discharge permit during the next heat wave. The) Tj
T*
(regional authority has issued a notice of concern, and a second excursion in the same) Tj
T*
(calendar year would trigger a formal compliance review. This report sets out the) Tj
T*
(retrofit options and recommends one.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
