(Constraints) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Four constraints shaped every option below, and they are listed in the order that ruled) Tj
T*
(candidates out.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The plant cannot be taken offline. There is no third basin and no equalisation storage,) Tj
T*
(so one basin must remain in service at all times. Any retrofit has to be installed one) Tj
T*
(basin at a time, with the working basin carrying the full load for the duration. The) Tj
T*
(plant's hydraulic model shows a single basin can carry peak flow for no more than 14) Tj
T*
(consecutive days before solids carry over into the clarifiers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The budget is 1.4 million dollars, approved in the current capital cycle. Funds not) Tj
T*
(committed by the end of the fiscal year return to the general reserve and would have to) Tj
T*
(be requested again.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The existing basin floor cannot carry additional dead load. A 1994 structural assessment) Tj
T*
(limits any new fixed equipment on the floor slab to 40 kilograms per square metre.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Finally, the retrofit must not increase the plant's electrical demand. The site's) Tj
T*
(service connection is already at 92 percent of its rated capacity, and upgrading it) Tj
T*
(would require a new transformer and a separate utility agreement that takes 18 months.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
