(Options considered) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Replacing the diffuser grid with fine-bubble membrane diffusers is the recommended) Tj
T*
(option. Fine-bubble units transfer oxygen at about 2.8 kilograms per kilowatt-hour, more) Tj
T*
(than double the present grid, which both restores the dissolved oxygen margin and lowers) Tj
T*
(blower demand. Installation fits the 14-day single-basin window, and the units mount on) Tj
T*
(the existing floor supports at 22 kilograms per square metre.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Mechanical surface aerators were ruled out on electrical demand. Four units sized for) Tj
T*
(Basin 2 would add 150 kilowatts, pushing the site past its service capacity and) Tj
T*
(triggering the transformer upgrade and its 18-month utility agreement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A third aeration basin was ruled out on both cost and schedule. The lowest construction) Tj
T*
(estimate received was 3.2 million dollars, more than twice the approved budget, and the) Tj
T*
(earliest completion date was 26 months away. It remains the right answer if the service) Tj
T*
(area grows past 60,000 residents, and the site plan reserves land for it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Chemical oxygen dosing was ruled out as an ongoing cost rather than a fix. It would meet) Tj
T*
(the permit floor during excursions but adds an estimated 180,000 dollars a year in) Tj
T*
(reagent, against a one-off retrofit, and does nothing about the fouled grid.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
